  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 4, 'The added value of “collect once, use for many purposes” principle'. Five stacked tiers rise from a person icon at the base. Bottom to top: Primary, individual data collection (clinical, lab, pharmacy, registries and ID data); Person-centred health service delivery (clinical decision support, scheduling, case management); Programme management (operational decision support, quality improvement, facility management, process optimization); Health system monitoring (national strategic plans and policies, national indicators, accountability); and Global monitoring (accountability towards the SDGs). A side bar groups the lower two tiers as 'Primary data use' and the upper three as 'Secondary data use'.",
